      "message": "feat(sim,app): plasma laws at the post gate - CL reader, cut crossing, enclosure from the rings, cover law\n\nStep 2 of the plasma through-cut laws (#672, part of #621):\n\n- sim::verify::plasma is a directory module: `PlasmaProgram::from_toolpath`\n  reads the laws' input from `Toolpath::plasma` (the torch spans, arcs\n  chorded at 0.01 mm, the torch-off travel as the rapid into each cut) -\n  never re-parsed text; a path without a record, or with one off its\n  moves, is refused by name.\n- The gate: `posting::plasma_clause` runs inside `verification_report`,\n  so a plasma refusal blocks the post (\"post blocked - Plasma1: plasma\n  cut order: ...\") on every surface; the not-judged line SAYS the 3D\n  stock sim does not run for plasma and that the 2D laws judged the op\n  (clean, or the warnings named). An op with no path, or a path with no\n  record, is a blocking problem of its own.\n- Laws: cut crossing (a ring through an earlier ring - the 2D gouge)\n  refuses; enclosure is recomputed from the rings and a PARENT the\n  geometry disagrees with is refused by name; `small` only on INNER; a\n  one-point cut without `small` is \"no cut path\"; an open-run parent and\n  a closed cut that never closes are malformed; a rapid leaving from a\n  freed part's edge is not a tip-up.\n- motion::plasma::laws: the cover law (#676 decision 12) refuses by name\n  a slot, notch or inside corner narrower than the kerf that the offset\n  bridged instead of cutting (any contour point farther than one kerf\n  width from its own lit chords); `kerf_law` moved beside it.\n- The 1300PL check's note names where the through-cut is judged.\n\nPinned by sim plasma_laws (15), sim plasma_program (5), motion\nplasma::tests (12, incl. a_slot_narrower_than_the_kerf_is_refused_not_bridged),\napp plasma_gate (4), plasma_machine, plasma_profile, post_not_judged.\n\nFixes #672\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
