      "message": "fix(sim,motion): plasma laws judge corner hits and collinear rings; inside corners keep their tip\n\nReview of #791:\n\n- Tip-up: a rapid in or out of a freed part through one of its corners\n  never crossed an edge properly, so it went unjudged. The rapid is now\n  split at every contact with the ring (a proper crossing, a vertex it\n  passes through, the ends of a stretch along an edge) and judged piece\n  by piece: a piece whose midpoint lies strictly inside the part is a\n  tip-up. A rapid leaving the part's own edge outward stays clear.\n- Cut crossing: two overlapping rings meeting only at vertices or along\n  collinear edges never crossed properly and only the torch-height\n  warning fired. A later ring with a piece strictly inside the earlier\n  ring and one strictly outside it is now refused; a shared edge with\n  nothing entering (common-line cutting) stays legal.\n- Cover law: every inside corner leaves a kerf-radius tip the torch\n  cannot reach, so the law exempts each inside corner's tip zone -\n  r (tan(delta/2) - sqrt 3) along each wall, what even the ideal miter\n  path leaves beyond 2r; empty from 60 degrees up - and judges only the\n  material beyond it. Sharp V-notches generate; the 1 mm notch and\n  keyway are still refused, and the refusal names the gap it measured\n  against the kerf.\n\nPinned by sim plasma_laws::a_rapid_through_a_freed_parts_corner_is_a_tip_up,\nplasma_laws::an_overlapping_ring_meeting_only_at_vertices_and_edges_is_refused\nand motion plasma::tests::a_sharp_inside_corner_generates_with_its_tip_left_not_refused.\n\nRefs #672\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
