        "date": "2026-11-11T08:09:31Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(sim,motion): a part inside an earlier one touching its edge crosses it; cap the corner tip zone at a kerf\n\nDelta review of #791:\n- rings_cross: a later ring with a piece strictly inside an earlier\n  ring crosses it unless it is wholly, strictly enclosed - \"inside AND\n  outside\" missed square(0,0,50) then [0,25]x[0,50], whose x=25 edge runs\n  through the freed part (only the kerf warning fired). Shared edges and\n  a hole touching its outline at a vertex stay legal.\n- tip_zone: the exempt zone r(tan(d/2) - sqrt3) is capped at one kerf\n  width (2r, the 30 deg zone); a non-finite tan takes the cap. Uncapped,\n  deep narrow V-slots (4 deg x 20 mm and the like) and a zero-width slit\n  generated silently with the feature uncut.\n- uncovered: on a slot floor the named gap is the smaller of the nearest\n  non-adjacent edge and the floor's length (the width, not the depth).\n\nPinned by a_ring_inside_an_earlier_part_touching_its_edge_is_refused\n(sim plasma_laws) and a_deep_narrow_wedge_is_refused_not_exempted_as_a_corner_tip\n(motion plasma::tests). Decision 4a and the cut-crossing entry updated.\n\nRefs #672\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
